\cf0 \ul \ulc0 Data Set Description
\f1\b0 \ulnone \
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 This data set contains information about 882 non-directed crisis dyads identified from the main data collections offered by the International Crisis Behavior Project. The data set spans the years 1918-2001. A crisis dyad is a pair of states satisfying each of the following three conditions: (1) both are members of the interstate system, (2) at least one of the states satisfies all three of the ICB necessary conditions for crisis involvement, and (3) at least one of the states has directed a hostile action against the other. Each case in this data set represents an annual observation of each of the crisis dyads over the complete duration of their confrontation. For more information about the construction of this data set, as well as a comparison of crisis dyads to militarized interstate dispute dyads, see Hewitt (2003).\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \ul \ulc0 Variable Descriptions
\f1\b0 \ulnone \
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \
1.	CRISNO
\f1\b0  \'96 ICB crisis-level ID number corresponding to the crisis from which dyad was identified..\
\

\f0\b 2.	YEAR
\f1\b0  \'96 Year of crisis dyad-year observation\
\

\f0\b 3.	CRISNAME
\f1\b0  \'96 Crisis name\
\

\f0\b 4.	STATEA
\f1\b0  \'96 3-digit COW ID number for state A.\
\

\f0\b 5.	NAMEA
\f1\b0  \'96 3-letter abbreviation for state A.\
\

\f0\b 6.	ACTNUMA
\f1\b0  \'96 ICB actor-level sequence number (variable CRACNO in the actor-level ICB data set) for state A. This ID number corresponds to the actor\'92s case number in the actor-level ICB data set . If state A is not considered a crisis-actor by ICB, then ACTNUMA equals 9999.\
\

\f0\b 7.	STATEB
\f1\b0  \'96 3-digit COW ID number for state B.\
\

\f0\b 8.	NAMEB
\f1\b0  \'96 3-letter abbreviation for state B.\
\

\f0\b 9.	ACTNUMB
\f1\b0  \'96 ICB actor-level sequence number (variable CRACNO in the actor-level ICB data set) for state B. See ACTNUMA, variable 6, for more detail.\
 \

\f0\b 10.	ONESIDE
\f1\b0  \'96 Indicates whether the crisis dyad is one-sided or not. \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li1080\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 0 \'96 two sided dyad (both dyad members are considered crisis actors)\
1 \'96 one-sided dyad, state A is a non-crisis actor\
2 \'96 one-sided dyad, state B is a non-crisis actor\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 11.	COWMEMA
\f1\b0  \'96 Indicates the interstate system membership status of state A according to the Correlates of War Project\'92s criteria.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-360\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 0 \'96	state is a member of interstate system for entire duration of crisis dyad period (if a state terminates on the last day of the crisis period, it is considered an independent state for the entire duration of the crisis dyad period)\
\pard\pardeftab720\li1080\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 1 \'96 state started during crisis dyad period \
2 \'96 state terminated during crisis dyad period (before last day of crisis)\
3 \'96 state started after termination of crisis dyad period\
4 \'96 state terminated before initiation of crisis dyad period\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 12.	COWMEMB
\f1\b0  \'96 Indicates the interstate system membership status of state B according to the Correlate\'92s of War Project\'92s criteria (coding rules are the same as for COWMEMA, variable 11 above).\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 13.	GWMEMA
\f1\b0  \'96 Indicates the interstate system membership status of state A according to Gleditsch and Ward\'92s (1999) criteria.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-360\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 0 \'96	state is a member of interstate system for entire duration of crisis dyad period (if a state terminates on the last day of the crisis period, it is considered an independent state for the entire duration of the crisis dyad period)\
\pard\pardeftab720\li1080\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 1 \'96 state started during crisis dyad period \
2 \'96 state terminated during crisis dyad period (before last day of crisis)\
3 \'96 state started after termination of crisis dyad period\
4 \'96 state terminated before initiation of crisis dyad period\
5 \'96 state is a microstate\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 14.	GWMEMB
\f1\b0  \'96 Indicates the interstate system membership status of state B according to Gleditsch and Ward\'92s (1999) criteria (coding rules are the same as for GWMEMA, variable 13 above).\
\

\f0\b 15.
\f1\b0 	
\f0\b IWCA
\f1\b0  \'96 The ICB actor-level coding for whether the crisis for state A was an intra-war crisis. The coding below is the same as ICB\'92s coding in the actor-level data set. If an actor is not a crisis actor, IWCA equals \'9699.\
\pard\tx-720\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\tx-720\pardeftab720\li1080\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 1 -	not an intra-war crisis (IWC)\
\pard\tx-720\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-360\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 2 -	Entry of a major actor into an ongoing war
\f0\b  
\f1\b0 (Military campaigns in the Middle East by Germany and Italy triggered intra-war crises for Britain, Iraq and Vichy France in 1941).\
3 -	Perceived high probability of a major actor entering a war (Israel's crisis in November 1956 arose from the Soviet threat to intervene in the Suez Nationalization-War Campaign Crisis).\
\pard\tx-720\pardeftab720\li1080\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 4 -	Exit of a major actor \
\pard\tx-720\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-360\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 5 -	Perceived high probability of major power exiting a war (On 23 October 1972 South Vietnam learned of agreements reached between the U.S. and North Vietnam [the Paris Accords], which could have resulted in the exit of the U.S. from the War - in the Christmas Bombing Crisis).\
6 -	Technological escalation of a war (German aerial bombing of the U.K. in 1940 constituted the Battle of Britain intra-war crisis).
\f0\b \

\f1\b0 7 -	Major non-technological escalation
\f0\b  
\f1\b0 (On 30 March 1972 North Vietnam launched a spring offensive, initiating the Vietnam-Ports Mining intra-war crisis).
\f0\b \

\f1\b0 8 -	Defeat in a significant battle (The Soviet defeat of the German Army at the Battle of Stalingrad triggered an IWC for Germany).\
9 -	Internal deterioration
\f0\b  
\f1\b0 (In March 1944 Hungarian leaders perceived that German troops massing on its borders were about to occupy Hungary).\
\pard\tx-720\pardeftab720\li1080\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 10-Other\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \ul \ulc0   \ulnone \
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 16.
\f1\b0 	
\f0\b IWCB
\f1\b0  - The ICB actor-level coding for whether the crisis for state B was an intra-war crisis. The code rules are the same as for IWCA (variable 14 above). If an actor is not a crisis actor, IWCB equals \'9699.\
\

\f0\b 17.	YRTRIGA
\f1\b0  \'96 Year of crisis trigger for state A. When state A is a non-crisis actor, YRTRIGA is set to \'9699.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 18.	MOTRIGA
\f1\b0  \'96 Month of crisis trigger for state A. When state A is a non-crisis actor, MOTRIGA is set to \'9699. In some cases, the ICB Project was unable to identify the precise month of the trigger for a crisis actor. In those cases, it was assumed that the crisis had been triggered in December of the given year.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 19.	DATRIGA
\f1\b0  \'96 Day of crisis trigger for state A. When state A is a non-crisis actor, DATRIGA is set to \'9699. When the ICB Project was unable to identify the precise day of the trigger for a crisis actor, the following codes were used in the actor-level data set:\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li1080\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 66 \'96 trigger occurred in the first third of the given month\
77 \'96 trigger occurred in the middle third of the given month\
88 \'96 trigger occurred in the last third of the given month\
99 \'96 unable to estimate precisely when in the given month the crisis began\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
For the dyadic-level data set, the following assumptions were made to estimate DATRIGA:\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li1080\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 if DATRIGA=66, trigger occurs on the 10\super th\nosupersub  day of the given month\
if DATRIGA=77, trigger occurs on the 20\super th\nosupersub  day of the given month\
if DATRIGA=88 or 99, trigger occurs on the last day of the given month\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 20.	YRTERMA
\f1\b0  \'96 Year of crisis termination for state A. When state A is a non-crisis actor, YRTERMA is set to \'9699.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 21.	MOTERMA
\f1\b0  \'96 Month of crisis termination for state A. When state A is a non-crisis actor, MOTERMA is set to \'9699. When the ICB Project was unable to identify the precise month of the termination for a crisis actor, the same coding rules were applied as for MOTRIGA (variable 18, described above).\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 22.	DATERMA
\f1\b0  \'96 Day of crisis termination for state A. When state A is a non-crisis actor, DATERMA is set to \'9699. When the ICB Project was unable to identify the precise day of the crisis termination for a crisis actor, the same coding rules were applied as for DATRIGA (variable 19, described above).\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 23.	YRTRIGB
\f1\b0  \'96 Year of crisis trigger for state B. When state B is a non-crisis actor, YRTRIGB is set to \'9699.\
\

\f0\b 24.	MOTRIGB
\f1\b0  \'96 Month of crisis trigger for state B. When state B is a non-crisis actor, MOTRIGB is set to \'9699. When the ICB Project was unable to identify the precise month of the trigger for a crisis actor, the same coding rules were applied as for MOTRIGA (variable 18, described above).\
\

\f0\b 25.
\f1\b0 	
\f0\b DATRIGB
\f1\b0  \'96 Day of crisis trigger for state B. When state B is a non-crisis actor, DATRIGB is set to \'9699. When the ICB Project was unable to identify the precise day of the trigger for a crisis actor, the same coding rules were applied as for DATRIGA (variable 19, described above).\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 26.	YRTERMB
\f1\b0  \'96 Year of crisis termination for state B. When state B is a non-crisis actor, YRTERMB is set to \'9699.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 27.	MOTERMB
\f1\b0  \'96 Month of crisis termination for state B. When state B is a non-crisis actor, MOTERMB is set to \'9699. When the ICB Project was unable to identify the precise month of the termination for a crisis actor, the same coding rules were applied as for MOTRIGA (variable 18, described above).\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 28.	DATERMB
\f1\b0  \'96 Day of crisis termination for state B. When state B is a non-crisis actor, DATERMB is set to \'9699. When the ICB Project was unable to identify the precise day of the crisis termination for a crisis actor, the same coding rules were applied as for DATRIGA (variable 19, described above).\
\

\f0\b 29.	TRGYRDY
\f1\b0  \'96 Dyadic trigger year\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \ul \ulc0 A Note about Dyadic Trigger and Termination Dates\ulnone  - For two-sided crises, the dyadic trigger date is set to the later of the two trigger dates for the two dyad members. That is, the crisis dyad begins once both states cross the crisis threshold. The dyadic termination date is set to the earlier of the two termination dates for the actors. As soon as one of the countries in the dyad believes the crisis has terminated, the dyadic nature of the crisis is complete. For one-sided dyads, trigger and termination dates are obviously not available for the non-crisis actor. For these dyads, the dyadic trigger and termination dates are based solely on the trigger and termination dates for the sole crisis actor. \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 30.	TRGMODY
\f1\b0  \'96 Dyadic trigger month (See TRGYRDY, variable 29, for more information about how dyadic trigger and termination dates are calculated.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 31.	TRGDADY
\f1\b0  \'96 Dyadic trigger day (See TRGYRDY, variable 29, for more information about how dyadic trigger and termination dates are calculated.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0  \
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 32.	TRMYRDY
\f1\b0  \'96 Dyadic termination year (See TRGYRDY, variable 29, for more information about how dyadic trigger and termination dates are calculated.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 33.	TRMMODY
\f1\b0  \'96 Dyadic termination month (See TRGYRDY, variable 29, for more information about how dyadic trigger and termination dates are calculated.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 34.	TRMDADY
\f1\b0  \'96 Dyadic termination day (See TRGYRDY, variable 29, for more information about how dyadic trigger and termination dates are calculated.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 35.
\f1\b0 	
\f0\b DURDAYS
\f1\b0  \'96 Dyad duration, in days (For information on how estimates were made when the precise day or month for crisis triggers and terminations was not available, see entries for variables MOTRIGA and DATRIGA, variables 18 and 19, respectively.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 36.	DURYEAR
\f1\b0  \'96 Number of calendar years spanned by dyad\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 37.	ONGOING
\f1\b0  \'96 Indicates whether the crisis dyad-year represents a year subsequent to the calendar year in which the crisis dyad began.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li1080\ri0\partightenfactor0
\cf0 0 \'96 year of crisis onset\
1 \'96 ongoing crisis dyad-year (i.e. crisis began in a previous year)\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri0\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 38.	CRDYNUM
\f1\b0  \'96 Unique crisis dyad number. Note, a crisis dyad that spans more than one year retains the same value for CRDYNUM for each annual observation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\partightenfactor0
